No call to lz4's deprecated LZ4_resetStreamHC() in libarchive's lz4 writer.

One of this project's patches to libarchive, which every build (macOS, Linux and
Windows) applies with patch_libarchive (native/build-config.sh), to the libarchive
release pinned there, in the order that LIBARCHIVE_PATCHES there lists them. A build
fails if any hunk does not apply exactly (no fuzz), and scripts/check-native-updates.sh
will not propose a libarchive release that it does not apply to. See "The libarchive
patches" in native/BUILD.md.

The lz4 writer (archive_write_add_filter_lz4.c) no longer calls LZ4_resetStreamHC(),
which lz4 1.11.0 deprecates, so that compiling it does not warn. In lz4 1.11.1 that
function is LZ4_initStreamHC(s, sizeof(*s)) followed by setting the compression level
(lz4hc.c); in its place the writer makes the two calls that lz4hc.h names,
LZ4_initStreamHC(s, sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t)) and LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast(s, level),
which leave the stream in the same state. With an lz4 older than 1.9.0, which lacks
them, it still calls LZ4_resetStreamHC().

The change is marked LIBARCHIVE_NET_LZ4_INIT_STREAM_HC, the marker that
LIBARCHIVE_PATCHES gives this patch: patch_libarchive checks that every file the patch
changes has it.

--- a/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_lz4.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_write_add_filter_lz4.c
@@ -526,7 +526,21 @@
 		if (lz4->lz4_stream == NULL) {
 #if LZ4_VERSION_MAJOR >= 1 && LZ4_VERSION_MINOR >= 7
 			lz4->lz4_stream = LZ4_createStreamHC();
+#if LZ4_VERSION_NUMBER >= 10900
+			/*
+			 * LIBARCHIVE_NET_LZ4_INIT_STREAM_HC: lz4 1.11.0
+			 * deprecates LZ4_resetStreamHC(), which initialises the
+			 * state as sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t) bytes and then sets
+			 * the level. lz4hc.h names these two calls (lz4 1.9.0
+			 * and later) in its place: they do the same.
+			 */
+			LZ4_initStreamHC(lz4->lz4_stream,
+			    sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t));
+			LZ4_resetStreamHC_fast(lz4->lz4_stream,
+			    lz4->compression_level);
+#else
 			LZ4_resetStreamHC(lz4->lz4_stream, lz4->compression_level);
+#endif
 #else
 			lz4->lz4_stream =
 			    LZ4_createHC(lz4->in_buffer_allocated);
